X:1
T:Silverton Polka, The
T: Transcribed from sessions by Gavin Atkin. I think it's best as an un-dotted hornpipe as noted here, but it's more often 
T: played as a polka. I don't intend to note it out as a polka unless asked to do so! You will find other versions played
T:  and notated here and there, including the version included in Barry Callaghan's book Hardcore English.
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=180
